        <tr><th scope="row">OpenAI</th><td data-label="What for">Drawing Pro pages in high quality (HD) from your descriptions</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">openai.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Gumroad</th><td data-label="What for">Checkout, payments and license checks, and the kind of site that first sent you when you click a Pro button</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy" rel="noopener">gumroad.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Vercel</th><td data-label="What for">The site's previous server, which checks Pro tokens made before the move to Cloudflare</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" rel="noopener">vercel.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Upstash</th><td data-label="What for">The previous server's database: Pro tokens and purchase records from before the move</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://upstash.com/trust/privacy.pdf" rel="noopener">upstash.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Pinterest</th><td data-label="What for">Only if you press a Save to Pinterest link, which opens Pinterest with the address of that page. Pinterest also reads our public feed of printable pages</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/en/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">pinterest.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Google</th><td data-label="What for">The Gmail inbox for our email</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Forward Email</th><td data-label="What for">Forwarding mail sent to our address</td><td data-label="Privacy policy"><a href="https://forwardemail.net/en/privacy" rel="noopener">forwardemail.net</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Most of these companies are based in the United States, so your data may be processed there. We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul class="post-list-items">
    <li>Descriptions and images: not kept by us. Requests to Workers AI: not retained after the request, with the limited exceptions in Cloudflare's Workers AI data usage terms. Requests to OpenAI (Pro pages in high quality only): up to 30 days, under OpenAI's API data policy.</li>
    <li>Daily counters under the hash of your IP address or under your Gumroad sale ID: about two days after the last change. The monthly count of your HD pages under your Gumroad sale ID: about 40 days after the last change.</li>
    <li>Pro tokens in our database (token, email, Gumroad sale ID, date): about 400 days after you activate Pro, or until you sign out on that device.</li>
    <li>Purchase records (email, Gumroad sale ID, date): until a refund is reported or you ask us to delete them. Refund marks (sale ID only): about 400 days.</li>
    <li>Pages in your browser, and the word for the kind of site that sent you on this visit: until you close the tab. The word for the kind of site that first sent you: until you clear this site's data. Your Pro token in your browser: until you sign out or clear this site's data.</li>
    <li>Network logs of the site: kept by Cloudflare under its own policy. Workers Logs of the requests our server code handles: three days. Requests to the Pinterest feed: only the latest 60.</li>
    <li>Pro tokens, purchase records and refund marks on the previous server (Vercel, Upstash): the same periods as above. Its request logs: kept by Vercel for a limited time under its own policy.</li>
    <li>Purchase records: also kept by Gumroad under its own policy.</li>
    <li>Emails to us: until we delete them. Ask us and we will delete yours, unless we need it as a record of a payment or refund.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a> and we will reply within one month. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>ColoringPageMaker is made for adults: parents, teachers and sellers who make coloring pages, often for children to color. The free tier asks for no name, email address or account. The site is not meant to be used by children on their own, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you think a child has given us personal data, for example by buying Pro, email us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the site starts handling data differently, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Peak Apps Studio, <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
